course: dictionary
lesson: 8838
title: Shipmate and the clues around it
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A shipmate is a person who sails on the same ship as you. Read the sentence around the word to find the clues. «At Marseilles he feasted with old shipmates» tells you that they ate together in a port, so they were probably sailors who had worked on a ship with him.
explain: Words can also be used in a friendly way. Sailors sometimes call any fellow sailor «shipmate» to be friendly. The Sea Rat in The Wind in the Willows talks about «my shipmates», the men he sailed with on his old voyages, so the word shows that he remembers them fondly.
explain: Try a check. Swap in your own meaning: «he feasted with old people who sailed on the same ship». Does it still make sense? Yes, so you have understood shipmate correctly.
fact: A shipmate is a person who sails on the same ship as you.
fact: «Shipmate» can mean another sailor in the crew.
fact: «Old shipmates» means sailors you sailed with long ago.
fact: Sailors sometimes say «shipmate» as a friendly way of speaking to a fellow sailor.
fact: Marseilles is a big port in the south of France, where «he met old shipmates».
exercise: «At Marseilles he feasted with old shipmates.» What is a shipmate? | A child in the same school class | A cook who makes shellfish dishes | *A person who sails on the same ship as you | A stranger you meet at a market
exercise: Which word means a person who sails on the same ship as you? | olive | voyage | *shipmate | harbour
exercise: A sailor calls another sailor «shipmate» in a friendly way. What does this tell you? | The speaker is a fish | They are enemies on a ship | *The two of them are friendly fellow sailors | They have never met before
test: «He rested in the olive-woods above the blue sea, and at Marseilles he feasted with old shipmates.» Who are the shipmates? | *Old sailors who sailed with him before | Strangers who sell olives | People who live in the olive woods | Fishermen who never leave the harbour
test: «Sometimes I dream of the shell-fish of Marseilles, and wake up crying!» What does the word shipmate most likely suggest about the speaker's memories? | He has never been to France | *He remembers his old crewmates warmly | He hates the sea | He is a shellfish seller
exam: The Sea Rat says «my shipmates» when he talks about his old voyages. What does shipmate mean here? | A large port in France | A friendly word for the men he sailed with | *A person who sails on the same ship as him | A map of the sea
